"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[6789],{26789:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"schemaVersion":1,"locale":"en","slug":"09-pensiya-i-cel","title":"Lesson 09. Retirement and Goals: The Mathematics of Financial Independence","sourceFingerprint":"2c08709821d0454e594fbbe31911df6a06f275763b3c639cc2b1d7ab29ceaf39","blocks":[{"id":"b001","markdown":"**Chapter 9. Personal Retirement Capital: The Mathematics of Financial Independence**  \\n*Thoughtful reading time: 8 minutes*"},{"id":"b002","markdown":"> “True financial freedom is measured not by yachts and luxury cars, but by the time when you can completely stop working and not reduce your usual level of comfort by even a single ruble.”"},{"id":"b003","markdown":"## 1. State Benefits vs. Real Needs"},{"id":"b004","markdown":"Protective instruments and asset structure were examined in previous chapters. It is time to answer the fundamental question: what numerical benchmark are you building your portfolio for?"},{"id":"b005","markdown":"For the vast majority of investors, the ultimate benchmark is the ability to stop working as an employee or close a business on a certain day without the risk of finding themselves on the brink of poverty. Let us realistically assess what help the state pension system will provide in this scenario."},{"id":"b006","markdown":"According to official statistics from the Social Fund of Russia, as of May 2026, the average old-age pension was recorded at **25 399 ₽**. Meanwhile, the average accrued wage across the country, according to Rosstat calculations for July of the same year, reached **109 524 ₽**."},{"id":"b007","markdown":"```\\n[Average country-wide wage: 109 524 ₽] \\n============================================================ 100%"},{"id":"b008","markdown":"[Average pension from SFR: 25 399 ₽] \\n============ 23% of previous income\\n```"},{"id":"b009","markdown":"The ratio is obvious: state benefits provide only about **23% of the previous wage**. As a benchmark: the International Labour Organization (ILO) prescribes a replacement rate of at least 40% as a baseline minimum for social security."},{"id":"b010","markdown":"If a family is used to allocating a budget based on 100 000 ₽ per month, transitioning to state support means a fourfold drop in the standard of living. It is no wonder that out of 40.5 million pensioners, over 8.4 million people (one in five) are forced to continue working. The demographic structure of society is relentlessly shifting: the share of elderly citizens is growing, while the number of officially employed young professionals is declining. Relying on an increase in the generosity of the pay-as-you-go pension system in 15–25 years is an unjustified illusion."},{"id":"b011","markdown":"## 2. Long-Term Savings Program (PDS): State Co-Financing"},{"id":"b012","markdown":"The only instrument where the state directly tops up your balance with actual cash at the legislative level is the **Long-Term Savings Program (PDS)**, administered by non-state pension funds (NPFs)."},{"id":"b013","markdown":"### Program Mechanics:\\n* **Minimum contribution:** from 2 000 ₽ per calendar year.\\n* **State subsidy:** valid for the first 10 years of participation, the maximum amount of state support is **up to 36 000 ₽ annually**.\\n* **Co-financing tiers** (depends on official monthly earnings):\\n  * For salaries up to 80 000 ₽: 1:1 match (for every ruble contributed, the state adds a ruble);\\n  * For salaries from 80 000 to 150 000 ₽: 1:2 match (50 kopecks per ruble contributed);\\n  * For salaries over 150 000 ₽: 1:4 match (25 kopecks per ruble contributed).\\n* **Lock-in period:** capital is paid out without loss of subsidies 15 years after entering into the contract or upon reaching the age of 55 (for women) and 60 (for men). Early access to funds is permitted exclusively in critical situations (e.g., payment for high-tech medical treatment).\\n* **Guarantees:** The Deposit Insurance Agency (DIA) protects the principal of contributions and accrued income up to **2.8 million ₽**.\\n* **Tax benefits:** contributions are eligible for the unified investment deduction (up to 400 000 ₽ per year combined with IIS-3, refund of up to 52 000 – 88 000 ₽ depending on the personal income tax rate)."},{"id":"b014","markdown":"## \uD83E\uDDEE Calculation in the Notebook Margins: Efficiency of Contributions to PDS"},{"id":"b015","markdown":"**Input parameters:**\\nAn investor with an income of up to 80 000 ₽ per month contributes **3 000 ₽ monthly** (36 000 ₽ per year) to the PDS, maximizing the state co-financing cap."},{"id":"b016","markdown":"| Source of funds over 15 years | Amount in today\'s prices | Share of the final balance |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| Own contributions (15 years \xd7 36 000 ₽) | **540 000 ₽** | 42.9% |\\n| State subsidy (10 years \xd7 36 000 ₽) | **360 000 ₽** | 28.6% |\\n| NPF investment return (inflation + 4% per annum) | **359 833 ₽** | 28.5% |\\n| **Total capital in the account after 15 years** | **1 259 833 ₽** | **100%** |"},{"id":"b017","markdown":"> **Please note:** Contributing amounts in excess of 36 000 ₽ per year in hopes of receiving state support is pointless — the subsidy limit is capped at 36 000 ₽. The money is locked in for a long horizon, and the actual return depends on the conservative strategy of the NPF. The PDS serves as a solid addition, but cannot be the sole pillar of a long-term plan."},{"id":"b018","markdown":"## 3. Calculating Independent Capital: The “300–400 Rule”"},{"id":"b019","markdown":"It is advisable to carry out all calculations exclusively **in today\'s rubles**. This eliminates the need to forecast inflation a quarter of a century ahead: you operate with the purchasing power of money “here and now”."},{"id":"b020","markdown":"### Calculation Algorithm:"},{"id":"b021","markdown":"1. **Determine your desired budget.**  \\n   Take your current monthly expenses and adjust them for your post-retirement lifestyle (subtract office expenses and a paid-off mortgage, add a budget for healthcare and travel). Let\'s assume the target benchmark is **80 000 ₽ per month**."},{"id":"b022","markdown":"2. **Determine the safe withdrawal rate.**  \\n   The classic Trinity Study (1998) proved: if you withdraw **4% of capital** from a diversified portfolio in the first year, and then adjust this amount annually for inflation, the probability of capital preservation over a 30-year period exceeds 95%.  \\n   For the Russian market, a benchmark is OFZ-IN bonds (indexed to official inflation). Under tight monetary policy, the real zero-coupon yield of long OFZ-IN was in the 5.7–7.1% range above inflation. Over the long run, a safe withdrawal benchmark is considered to be **from 3% to 4% per year**.\\n   * **3% per year** — ultra-conservative strategy (high share of OFZ and LQDT liquidity funds);\\n   * **4% per year** — moderate strategy (balanced share of stocks and gold)."},{"id":"b023","markdown":"3. **Capital formula:**\\n   $$\\\\text{Capital} = \\\\text{Monthly Expenses} \\\\times (300 \\\\dots 400)$$\\n   * The **300** multiplier corresponds to a 4% annual withdrawal: $80\\\\,000 \\\\times 300 = \\\\mathbf{24\\\\text{ million ₽}}$.\\n   * The **400** multiplier corresponds to a 3% annual withdrawal: $80\\\\,000 \\\\times 400 = \\\\mathbf{32\\\\text{ million ₽}}$."},{"id":"b024","markdown":"## 4. Capital Accumulation Timelines"},{"id":"b025","markdown":"How many years will it take to reach the target amount with investment returns at **“inflation + 4% per annum”** in today\'s rubles?"},{"id":"b026","markdown":"| Monthly Contribution | Capital 24 million ₽ (4% rate) | Capital 32 million ₽ (3% rate) |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **30 000 ₽** | ~ 32 years | ~ 38 years |\\n| **50 000 ₽** | ~ 24 years | ~ 29 years |\\n| **70 000 ₽** | ~ 19 years | ~ 23 years |\\n| **100 000 ₽** | ~ 15 years | ~ 18 years |"},{"id":"b027","markdown":"### Three key rules of the distance:\\n1. **Marginal return of the initial steps:** Increasing the contribution from 30 000 to 50 000 ₽ saves a full 8 years of hard work. A step from 70 000 to 100 000 ₽ will cut the timeline by only 4 years.\\n2. **Family synergy effect:** Investing together allows you to combine your monthly contribution, instantly moving you several rows down the table.\\n3. **The importance of an intermediate finish line:** Even a portfolio covering 50% of monthly expenses provides unprecedented autonomy—the ability to work part-time or change careers without panic. The state pension and PDS also reduce the burden: every 10 000 ₽ in third-party payments reduces the required capital target by 3–4 million ₽."},{"id":"b028","markdown":"## ✍️ Step-by-step workshop: calculating a personal retirement plan"},{"id":"b029","markdown":"1. **Fix your baseline budget:** Determine the exact amount of monthly expenses required for living without working (for example, 70 000 ₽).\\n2. **Calculate the capital range boundaries:**\\n   * Lower threshold (4% withdrawal): $70\\\\,000 \\\\times 300 = 21\\\\,000\\\\,000\\\\text{ ₽}$.\\n   * Upper threshold (3% withdrawal): $70\\\\,000 \\\\times 400 = 28\\\\,000\\\\,000\\\\text{ ₽}$.\\n3. **Check your pension entitlements:** Log in to the Gosuslugi portal and request an individual account statement from the SFR to evaluate your accumulated individual pension coefficients (IPC).\\n4. **Set a manageable starting contribution:** Compare your free cash flow against the timeline table. If the calculation shows 30 years—start with regular, comfortable contributions, reviewing and increasing their size once a year."}],"terms":[{"id":"pravilo-4-procentov","term":"The 4% Rule","definition":"a safe annual withdrawal rate from capital that allows living off returns."},{"id":"pds","term":"LSP (Long-Term Savings Program)","definition":"a long-term savings program with state co-financing."},{"id":"gos-sofinansirovanie","term":"Co-financing","definition":"a state co-payment of up to 36,000 ₽ per year on personal contributions to the LSP."}],"quizzes":[{"id":"q1","q":"An investor plans to spend 60,000 ₽ per month in retirement in today\'s prices and adheres to a conservative strategy with an annual withdrawal rate of 3% (multiplier of 400). What amount of capital do they need to accumulate?","options":["18 million ₽","7.2 million ₽","24 million ₽"],"correct":1,"explanation":"C. **Explanation:** With an annual withdrawal rate of 3%, a multiplier of 400 is applied: $60\\\\,000 \\\\times 400 = 24\\\\,000\\\\,000\\\\text{ ₽}$. (A multiplier of 300 would yield 18 million ₽, which corresponds to a 4% withdrawal rate)."},{"id":"q2","q":"What is the maximum state co-financing amount an LSP participant can receive in a single calendar year with a monthly income of up to 80,000 ₽?","options":["52,000 ₽","36,000 ₽","12,000 ₽"],"correct":1,"explanation":"B. **Explanation:** Under the LSP law, the maximum annual state subsidy is capped at 36,000 ₽ during the first 10 years of participation in the program."},{"id":"q3","q":"How will the required amount of personal capital change if the investor expects a guaranteed state payout of 20,000 ₽ per month with a base withdrawal rate of 4% (multiplier of 300)?","options":["It will not change; state payouts are not taken into account","It will decrease by 6 million ₽","It will decrease by 2.4 million ₽"],"correct":1,"explanation":"B. **Explanation:** Each ruble of guaranteed third-party income reduces the personal capital requirement by the multiplier amount: $20\\\\,000 \\\\times 300 = 6\\\\,000\\\\,000\\\\text{ ₽}$."}],"officialSources":[]}')}}]);